<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morón de la Frontera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morón de la Frontera is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, south-east of the city of Seville. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> clan, the Banu Dammar, ruled it as a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> in the early 11th century until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid-of-seville">al-Mutadid of Seville</a> annexed it. Taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in the 13th century, it became a frontier town facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, and it is now the site of a Spanish air base also used by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moron-de-la-frontera.jpg" alt="Morón de la Frontera" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Undefined · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mor%C3%B3n_de_la_Frontera.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
